{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt12\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#present_tense\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">present</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#participle\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">participle</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#gerund\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">gerund</a> of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/run#English\" title=\"run\">run</a></i></span></span>"}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Adjective","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"Moving or advancing at a run.\n<ol><li>Of a horse, having a running gait; not a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/trotter\" title=\"trotter\">trotter</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pacer\" title=\"pacer\">pacer</a>.</li></ol>"},{"definition":"Of a horse, having a running gait; not a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/trotter\" title=\"trotter\">trotter</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pacer\" title=\"pacer\">pacer</a>."},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/present\" title=\"present\">Present</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/current\" title=\"current\">current</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>running</b> month"}],"examples":["<b>running</b> month"]},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/flowing\" title=\"flowing\">Flowing</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/easy\" title=\"easy\">easy</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/cursive\" title=\"cursive\">cursive</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>running</b> handwriting"}],"examples":["<b>running</b> handwriting"]},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/continuous\" title=\"continuous\">Continuous</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ongoing\" title=\"ongoing\">ongoing</a>; keeping along step by step.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"a <b>running</b> commentary, a <b>running</b> explanation, my <b>running</b> theory"}],"examples":["a <b>running</b> commentary, a <b>running</b> explanation, my <b>running</b> theory"]},{"definition":"Having a continuous design or pattern.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>running</b> bond<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">;</span> <b>running</b> ornament"}],"examples":["<b>running</b> bond<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">;</span> <b>running</b> ornament"]},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/consecutive\" title=\"consecutive\">Consecutive</a> .","parsedExamples":[{"example":"He won the title for three <b>running</b> years."}],"examples":["He won the title for three <b>running</b> years."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt23\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Extending by a slender climbing or trailing stem.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"a <b>running</b> vine"}],"examples":["a <b>running</b> vine"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt25\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Discharging <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pus\" title=\"pus\">pus</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"a <b>running</b> sore"}],"examples":["a <b>running</b> sore"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt27\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/discharge\" title=\"discharge\">Discharging</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/snot\" title=\"snot\">snot</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/mucus\" title=\"mucus\">mucus</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"a <b>running</b> nose"}],"examples":["a <b>running</b> nose"]}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Adverb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt87\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/consecutively\" title=\"consecutively\">Consecutively</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/in_a_row\" title=\"in a row\">in a row</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"Mom's strawberry jam won the blue ribbon at the Holland County Fair three years <b>running</b>."}],"examples":["Mom's strawberry jam won the blue ribbon at the Holland County Fair three years <b>running</b>."]}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"The action of the verb <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt104\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/run#English\" title=\"run\">run</a></i>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"His <b>running</b> of the business leaves something to be desired."}],"examples":["His <b>running</b> of the business leaves something to be desired."]},{"definition":"The activity of running as a form of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/exercise\" title=\"exercise\">exercise</a>, as a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/sport\" title=\"sport\">sport</a>, or for any other reason.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>Running</b> is good exercise."}],"examples":["<b>Running</b> is good exercise."]},{"definition":"That which runs or flows; the quantity of a liquid which flows in a certain time or during a certain operation.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"the first <b>running</b> of a still"}],"examples":["the first <b>running</b> of a still"]},{"definition":"The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/discharge\" title=\"discharge\">discharge</a> from an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ulcer\" title=\"ulcer\">ulcer</a> or other <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/sore\" title=\"sore\">sore</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt109\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> The act of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/run_errands\" title=\"run errands\">running errands</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"I'm gonna go out and do my <b>running</b>."}],"examples":["I'm gonna go out and do my <b>running</b>."]},{"definition":""},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\"></span> The dependence of measured value, typically a coupling constant, on the energy scale at which it is probed due to higher-order interaction terms and associated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/renormalization\" title=\"renormalization\">renormalization</a> issues becoming relevant; metaphorically, the \"running\" of the measurement from its limiting macroscopic value."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Preposition","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt209\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Approaching; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/about\" title=\"about\">about</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/roughly\" title=\"roughly\">roughly</a>. <span class=\"maintenance-line\" about=\"#mwt210\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">(Can we add an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Wiktionary:Example_sentences\" title=\"Wiktionary:Example sentences\">example</a> for this sense?)</span><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:Requests_for_example_sentences_in_English#RUNNING\" about=\"#mwt210\"><!--Chambers 1908-->"}]}],"fr":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"French","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt220\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/running_shoe\" title=\"running shoe\">running shoe</a>"}]}],"es":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"Spanish","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt223\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/running#English\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\">running</a></span>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/jogging\" title=\"jogging\">jogging</a>"}]}]}